Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||10-26-2001||09:56 PM||||Saw one of those cars on Car and Driver TV once. John himself couldn't break into the 10's. 6 psi in the rear drag slicks, 3/4 of the track covered with traction compound, bogging the launch all failed to get hooked up. I think he finally got 11.01 or something. <P>It did do 224 MPH. WOW!! It sounded like a jet going past the camera guy. By the time the camera guy turned around, the Vette was a small dot.<P>I think I have it recorded... might go dig it out now.||||reg||1
Z||000007||btoth||10-26-2001||10:26 PM||||We have Mallett Corvette here in Berea.  They were working on building the fastest Corvette in the world or something.  (Rumor I think.)<P>They supposedly have special Goodyears made for their cars.  I've only seen a few of them at car shows - turbo ones, superchangers, big wheels and brakes... all that stuff.  They do carbon fiber intakes and engine covers too.... just to make them look cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Everytime I see one I always say "there's something different about that Corvette, but I don't know what..."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That's the best part.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroKyle||10-26-2001||11:36 PM||||Which proves Vettes are better than Vipers. I finally win!!! LOL, and see other convinced people.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||10-27-2001||12:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SCCA FIERO:<BR><B>Saw one of those cars on Car and Driver TV once. John himself couldn't break into the 10's. 6 psi in the rear drag slicks, 3/4 of the track covered with traction compound, bogging the launch all failed to get hooked up. I think he finally got 11.01 or something. <P>It did do 224 MPH. WOW!! It sounded like a jet going past the camera guy. By the time the camera guy turned around, the Vette was a small dot.<P>I think I have it recorded... might go dig it out now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The Lingenfelter Corvette made that 10 second run with a bad clutch. In the issue of C&D that had the same test as the show. They explained that. The Corvette was also geared <I>really</I> low for the high speed test. They said that it would do 65 in first gear. Very sweet car, but I liked the looks and the sound of the King Snake more than the Vette. But would take the Vette over the viper anyday.<P>The Mallet Corvette is a stroked 377 or so cid motor that's turbo'd and also does more than 200.||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||10-27-2001||12:03 PM||||Aren't the new Corvettes supposed to use a variable vale timming system co-developed by Toyota or something??||||reg||1
Z||000011||Shaft||10-27-2001||06:31 PM||||If they use any type of variable valve setup it's most likely to be the design they unvailed at the same time as the Caddy v-12. It has duel cams, but overhead valves. One cam sits on top of the other inside of the block, similar to the Mercedes V-8 that won indy some years back. Slammed Fiero posted something about this engine a while ago.||||reg||1
